## The rule, in one line

**One serving machine: free, for any purpose, with no licence file at all.**
**Two or more serving machines managed together: commercial licence required.**

A company running its production inference on one serving machine pays nothing
and is fully licensed. That is intended.

The legal line and the technical gate are the same line, on purpose. There is
no state where the software runs normally but you are quietly in breach. **If
it runs, you are licensed.**

## What counts as a machine

LMDS counts **serving machines** — machines that can actually run a model
(a working `llama-server`, or Docker plus at least one NVIDIA GPU). LMDS
detects this itself from what is present on the machine.

- **A control-plane hub with no engine does not count.** The machine you plan
  on, generate bundles on, push from and open the web console on is free.
  **So "hub + one serving node" is one machine.**
- **GPUs are not machines.** One computer with 8 GPUs is one machine.
- **Containers are not machines.** Many models on one machine is still one.
- **VMs and cloud instances are machines.** Eight serving VMs on one box is
  eight, not one.
- **Replacing a machine is not adding one**, provided the old one stops
  serving within 30 days.
- The count is the **most machines serving at the same time**, not a running
  total over time.

**The limit is on machines managed together** — machines in one inventory,
deployed to, pushed to, cloned between or monitored from one place. **Two
separate installations that each manage only their own single machine are each
free.** That is a deliberate boundary, not an oversight: anyone who wants a
cluster, or simply wants to run more than one machine from one place, needs
them managed together, and that is where the licence applies.

`LMDS_ROLE=hub` exists so you can correct a wrong detection. Using it to hide a
machine that really does serve models is a breach, even though it works — and
LMDS records whether a role was forced, so it is not hidden.

## If LMDS spots another LMDS on your network

LMDS may tell you that another LMDS installation is present on the same local
network — *"found another LMDS at 10.0.0.5"*. Three things about that, all of
them binding terms in `LICENSE` §1.6 rather than behaviour that might change:

- **Local detection only. Nothing is reported to us.** No information about
  your machines, network, models or usage is sent anywhere. LMDS has no
  telemetry, the licence introduces none, and this is not a channel for any.
- **It is information, not enforcement.** It blocks nothing and changes
  nothing about what you may do.
- **Finding another installation does not mean you are over the limit.**
  Separate installs that are not managed together are compliant — two
  independent installs on one network are each free. The message means only
  that another LMDS is there, in case you would like them to work as one
  fleet. It is never a statement that you are in breach.

## Free 30-day trial — issued automatically

Want to try a fleet, or try stacked multi-machine deployment? **Stacked needs
two machines by definition**, so you will need a trial licence to evaluate it.

**Ask and the system issues one immediately** — unlimited machines, 30 days,
**no human in the loop and no payment details.**

**Cooldown:** after a trial expires, the next one is issued **7 days later**.
During those 7 days your limit is one machine for **new** operations, and
nothing you are running is switched off (below). Need longer than 30 days? Ask
— we will arrange an extension rather than make you wait out a cooldown.

## Nothing running is ever switched off

When a trial lapses, or during a cooldown, you return to the free one-machine
tier **for new operations only**. Every model already deployed **keeps
running**, on every machine, and `start`, `stop`, `restart`, `logs`, `ps`,
`doctor` and `status` keep working on all of them — including automatic start
at boot.

A machine that reboots at 3am after a trial expired yesterday comes back up.
This is a term of the licence, not a promise.

## Always free, at every tier

Quality gates, `doctor`, `repair`, `validate`, `preflight`, secret redaction,
allowlists and approval prompts are never behind a paywall, at any tier.
We limit **scale**, never **safety**.

